id: pm-b8hwfr
title: "Bun event streaming falls back to authoritative history without node:sqlite"
description: "Packed bunx --bun can initialize and mutate a workspace, but pm events fails with event_index_unavailable because Bun exposes no Node DatabaseSync constructor. Preserve SQLite acceleration on Node while adding a bounded authoritative history-stream fallback with filter, ordering, cursor, provenance, and limit parity so the universal event surface remains functional under Bun."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[5]: "area:cli","area:sdk","github-pr:1053",mutation-events,"runtime:bun"
created_at: "2026-08-17T08:29:34.248Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-17T08:52:54.678Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-17T08:52:53.824Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-17T08:52:53.824Z"
author: "harness:codex"
parent: pm-ez1dfg
resolution: "Added index-equivalent authoritative history scanning for runtimes without node:sqlite, routed SDK event reads to it, and exposed a truthful authoritative_history source receipt."
expected_result: "Packed Node and Bun consumers can read, filter, paginate, resume, and follow mutation events with identical contracts regardless of SQLite availability."
actual_result: "Focused tests, exact full coverage, contracts, typecheck, ESLint, and real packed bunx --bun init/create/events acceptance pass; Node retains the derived SQLite path."
fixed_version: unreleased
