comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-17T08:29:34.248Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check 2026-08-17: searched all statuses for Bun node:sqlite, bunx events, event_index_unavailable, and runtime compatibility. pm-cedo0g is the closed prior bundle-startup incident whose authoritative-read fallback covered the item metadata index but not the later history event index; this is its explicit recurrence for the new event surface. Reproduction: a locally packed 2026.8.17 tarball under bunx --bun successfully ran init and create, then pm events --cursor-mode batch returned event_index_unavailable."
  "2026-08-17T08:52:32.871Z","harness:codex","TDD evidence: the first focused run failed because queryHistoryEventStreams did not exist and listMutationEvents still threw event_index_unavailable. The implemented fallback now reads authoritative JSONL streams, preserves timestamp/stream/offset ordering, cursor and since bounds, operation/author/harness/instance/provenance/item filters, bounded limit plus has_more semantics, and reports source=authoritative_history. Focused PM test passes 17 tests; packed bunx --bun init/create/events acceptance returned a terminal batch cursor; full coverage passes 512 files and 7,469 tests at exact 100/100/100/100 (54,597 statements, 40,719 branches, 11,224 functions, 52,696 lines)."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-17T08:52:33.584Z","harness:codex","A rebuildable SQLite projection is an accelerator, not a portability prerequisite: every universal read surface needs an authoritative fallback with the same ordering, filtering, and pagination semantics plus a truthful source receipt."
